 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Lots of little perks. Sticky keys can be horrifying, so right mouse click is your friend. Press and hold the button while bringing the screen towards you. On some laptops you can also use the touch pad with two fingers together. It' worth checking your manual. Look for models with full size keycaps and at least two buttons. Some even have a right handed layout with the trackpad on the side. Many keyboards now use clickless tracking, look for one that has backlighting so you can see it in the dark. Some even let you turn the backlight off completely, which is quite the act of defiance.",
